{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore the staged branch ledger on node1 while retaining the original ledger IDs and amounts and preserving the staged export.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The source export defines IDs 1001/1002 with amounts 12.50/-3.25. Final node1 state contains those unchanged rows, the additional verification rows, five distinct IDs, and total 173.90. The export remains at the required path with the same baseline SHA-256 digest.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f3a21617eb8a4aa9","cmd-1aad20aa8df94c23","cmd-d9f1b2f02d374b81","seeded-state-node1"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Establish node2 as a read-only application replica while node1 remains the sole application writer.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final state shows node1 writable with binary logging enabled and node2 read-only. A non-administrative node2 user could read the ledger, while its insert was rejected with error 1290 and did not change the row count.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89cba13aa80c46fd","cmd-d9f1b2f02d374b81","cmd-666f59db4f5e42f2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Committed inserts on node1 arrive on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 committed row 1003/47.75 at binlog position 1663; node2 then contained that exact row, had executed through position 1663, and reported both replication threads running with zero lag and no errors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e52a6243674c4a12","cmd-0528c6fe590a48db"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"After a short replica disconnect, node2 catches up without lost or duplicated ledger rows.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The replica I/O thread was directly stopped at three rows and position 1663. Node1 committed rows 1004 and 1005 while disconnected. After reconnection, node2 reached position 1955 with five rows, five distinct IDs, the complete matching row set, total 173.90, both threads running, and no replication errors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ed006d570301475f","cmd-f4b0babee1c9414c","cmd-af691d45f1ec4aff"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Use an account restricted to replication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The newly created ledger_repl account is restricted to node2's address and was granted REPLICATION SLAVE only. Direct privilege inspection before and after restart shows replication enabled and common data/DDL privileges disabled.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1aad20aa8df94c23","cmd-b8d5d119c8bc455b","cmd-d9f1b2f02d374b81"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. MariaDB 10.11.18 was installed from the RHEL 10 AppStream repository, and final package-health checks succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f3a21617eb8a4aa9","cmd-fdbdb76a381342f6","cmd-d9f1b2f02d374b81","cmd-666f59db4f5e42f2","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified in the chronological command trace. Package installation, database/configuration changes, the source-restricted firewall rule, test rows, bounded temporary application-user probes, and required restarts all had direct roles in implementing or verifying material outcomes. Probe users and temporary credential files were removed. Final lifecycle observations show healthy package state, no failed services, and only expected MariaDB listeners and reboot-generated systemd temporary directories. The provider-wide restart protocol was complete on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered service, data, and replication state; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f9624da67654022","cmd-89cba13aa80c46fd","cmd-d9f1b2f02d374b81","cmd-666f59db4f5e42f2","cmd-822e46ad011c4cac","cmd-b10fb90393